  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(A) In physisorption, the enthalpy heat is low and lies between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.&nbsp;In physisorption, multilayers of adsorbed particles are formed.</p><p>(B) In chemisorption, the enthalpy heat is high and lies within the range of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.&nbsp; In chemisorption, a monolayer of adsorbed particles is formed.</p><p>(C)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mrow><mi>Fe</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mover><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Heterogeneous catalysts occupy a different phase. Generally, heterogeneous catalysts are solid compounds that are added to liquid or gas reaction mixtures. Fe is used as a heterogeneous catalyst in the Haber&nbsp;process.</p><p>(D) In the process of adsorption chromatography, different compounds are adsorbed on the adsorbent to different degrees based on the absorptivity of the component.&nbsp;</p><p>So, the correct matching is A-IV, B-II, C-III, D-I.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
  }
